From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:53:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sync: Keep sessions stable across reconnects

The request manager resends outstanding mutations with their original
request IDs after reconnecting, but each WebSocket connection currently
gets a fresh session ID. A successful mutation whose response is lost can
therefore be executed again because its (session ID, request ID)
deduplication key changes.

Generate the session ID once per WebSocket worker and reuse it in every
Connect message. Separate clients still get independent sessions.

Add a local WebSocket fixture that models committed mutation results and
drops two responses. Verify the mutation is applied once, its request and
session stay stable, and independently created clients have distinct
sessions.
---
 src/sync/web_socket_manager.rs |   9 +-
 tests/reconnect.rs             | 162 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 169 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 tests/reconnect.rs

